text: >-
  To begin early on Wednesday morning, it was said that Robinson drove to UVU
  very early

  making a three hour drive by around 8:30 am. It was also said that Robinson
  left a message

  under Robinson's keyboard that was set out in full in the search warrants,
  suggesting that

  Robinson had spent the night with Twiggs (apparently in River Road), meaning
  that he must

  have been gone by the time that Twiggs awoke. The next time they communicated
  was around

  6:30 pm when Robinson was trying to retrieve his rifle for the second time. It
  was only at this

  point that Twiggs received a message telling him to look under the keyboard.
